      <data key="data">When car dealer Charlie Babbitt learns that his estranged father has died, he returns home to Cincinnati, where he discovers that he has a savant older brother named Raymond and that his father&#x27;s $3 million fortune is being left to the mental institution in which Raymond lives. Motivated by his father&#x27;s money, Charlie checks Raymond out of the facility in order to return with him to Los Angeles. The brothers&#x27; cross-country trip ends up changing both their lives.</data>
