      <data key="data">Against formidable odds -- and an old-school diving instructor embittered by the U.S. Navy&#x27;s new, less prejudicial policies -- Carl Brashear sets his sights on becoming the Navy&#x27;s first African-American master diver in this uplifting true story. Their relationship starts out on the rocks, but fate ultimately conspires to bring the men together into a setting of mutual respect, triumph and honor.</data>
