      <data key="data">Richard Martin buys a gift, a new NDR-114 robot. The product is named Andrew by the youngest of the family&#x27;s children. &quot;Bicentennial Man&quot; follows the life and times of Andrew, a robot purchased as a household appliance programmed to perform menial tasks. As Andrew begins to experience emotions and creative thought, the Martin family soon discovers they don&#x27;t have an ordinary robot.</data>
